1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,580
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,210
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:07,850
(Episode 67)

5
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,220
Kang Hae Ra.

6
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,380
Have you lost your mind?

7
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:40,310
We're at work.

8
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,020
Who did you meet today?

9
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,960
What business is it of yours
who I meet?

10
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:53,690
Kim Chun Hee,

11
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:55,860
my former cellmate.

12
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:57,660
You really don't know?

13
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,870
How would I know
your prison buddies?

14
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:04,770
Why should I care?

15
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:10,740
Kang Hae Ra.

16
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,710
Are you scared?

17
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:17,450
What?

18
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:20,150
If you aren't, ask me to my face.

19
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:24,020
If you go behind my back
and get caught,

20
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:29,090
you'd better brace yourself
for what comes next.

21
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:37,900
I outrank you.

22
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,140
I lead the Design Team at Cheongma.

23
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:43,370
Seeing her today...

24
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:45,410
must've given you
an idea of my past.

25
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,010
My life has been much rougher
than you think.

26
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:53,420
So...

27
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:56,690
be careful while I still treat you
as my superior.

28
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:59,890
Do that, and I'll continue
to show you respect.

29
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:02,390
Are you threatening me right now?

30
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:03,900
You catch on fast.

31
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:06,530
So...

32
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:09,000
stop...

33
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,700
pushing your luck.

34
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:18,080
Got it, Ms. Kang?

35
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:26,720
Hey. Ko Eun Seol!

36
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,320
I know you must be tired after work,

37
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:36,690
but I just had to talk
to you today, Eun Seol.

38
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:40,400
What I said the other day
really shocked you, didn't it?

39
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:41,670
Yes.

40
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:45,540
You looked so troubled I couldn't
bring myself to press you further.

41
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,470
And I couldn't tell Eun Guk
anything either.

42
00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:49,170
It drove me crazy.

43
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:52,610
I was so worried
I couldn't even focus on my work.

44
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,350
I'm sorry.

45
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:01,450
You know what?
I'm just going to tell you.

46
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,850
Is that okay?

47
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:04,590
Of course.

48
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:06,520
I can keep a secret.

49
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:09,460
Whatever you say,
my lips are sealed.

50
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:12,230
So,

51
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,930
did you find your birth mother?

52
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:18,600
I found someone
who's almost certainly her,

53
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,570
but I haven't been able
to tell her yet.

54
00:03:21,770 --> 00:03:22,810
Why not?

55
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:24,310
She might've spent
all these years...

56
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:26,040
desperately searching for you
after the adoption.

57
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:28,980
No, that's not possible.

58
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,180
And you know how it is.

59
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:33,890
Know what?

60
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:37,590
My past hasn't been smooth sailing.

61
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:43,290
The rough life I've lived...

62
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:47,630
would just be too much
for my birth parents to bear.

63
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,340
Eun Seol...

64
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,270
So I made up my mind.

65
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,470
Rather than revealing the truth,

66
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:58,840
I'm going to protect
my birth mother.

67
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,880
Protect your birth mother?

68
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:02,580
Then...

69
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:05,120
she must be someone close to you.

70
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,520
Is she really?

71
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:09,150
Yes, that's right.

72
00:04:09,590 --> 00:04:12,790
Then you should go to her right now
and tell her the truth.

73
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,830
That's how parents are.

74
00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:18,760
They open their hearts wider
to a child who's hurting.

75
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:23,030
So go to your parents right now
and tell them everything, okay?

76
00:05:08,450 --> 00:05:11,650
Outside, my team will be on standby.

77
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:14,820
It'll only take an hour
to work on his phone.

78
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:32,540
Secretary Choi, is that your lunch?

79
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,910
Yes. I didn't have much
of an appetite.

80
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:40,040
I ate alone today, too.
Why didn't you say something?

81
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:42,310
Eun Seol,

82
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:44,550
I'm always the one
who reaches out first.

83
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,320
You're right about that.

84
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:51,220
Let me treat you
to something really good.

85
00:05:51,860 --> 00:05:53,660
What's your favorite food,
Secretary Choi?

86
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:56,830
A home-cooked meal?

87
00:05:58,430 --> 00:05:59,530
Yes, a home-cooked meal.

88
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,300
Eating out all the time
gets old fast.

89
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:05,000
Maybe it's because I grew up
in an orphanage,

90
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:08,670
but nothing beats a warm,
home-cooked meal made just for me.

91
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:10,370
Well,

92
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:12,240
I've always wondered
what that would feel like.

93
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:18,120
No problem.
I'll whip you up a home-cooked meal.

94
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:19,680
Really?

95
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,490
You mean it? No backing out later.

96
00:06:23,290 --> 00:06:24,290
Nice.

97
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:28,290
By the way,
why are you always so nice to me?

98
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,360
No special reason.

99
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:32,400
You feel like
a younger brother to me.

100
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:45,180
Here are the survey results
from the store event.

101
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,240
Take a look.

102
00:06:47,350 --> 00:06:48,350
All right.

103
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:55,190
The CEO goes
to the sauna a lot, right?

104
00:06:55,850 --> 00:06:57,720
Yes. 2 or 3 times a week.

105
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,460
What time does he usually go?

106
00:07:01,030 --> 00:07:03,260
If he's free, he hits the sauna
before coming home.

107
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:04,860
Sometimes he goes to sober up.

108
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,430
Is that so?

109
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:09,430
Don't tell me you're planning
to go with him.

110
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:11,970
I need to make an effort,

111
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,570
especially since I should
be thankful he finally accepted me.

112
00:07:14,910 --> 00:07:16,370
How's your mother doing?

113
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:18,810
She seems very comfortable
staying with her caregiver.

114
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:19,910
Yes.

115
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:22,150
Knowing she's comfortable there
puts my mind at ease, too.

116
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:25,920
While she's there, she might
as well take a good, long rest.

117
00:07:28,890 --> 00:07:32,860
You can focus more on work,
and your mother is comfortable.

118
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,460
It works out well for everyone.

119
00:07:35,990 --> 00:07:38,460
Since she's already there,
I told her to stay a bit longer.

120
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:44,700
I have to move in with your family
once we're married anyway.

121
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,940
We both need to practice
living apart.

122
00:07:48,570 --> 00:07:50,880
Really? Do you mean that?

123
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,850
Seok Jin,
I'll be so much better to you.

124
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,620
It's about So Yeon.

125
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,450
Did Chief Cha mention...

126
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,490
which hospital
she's transferring to?

127
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,930
He just said she won't
be receiving treatment for now.

128
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:09,860
He didn't mention any hospital.

129
00:08:12,330 --> 00:08:15,170
How can he just neglect someone
who's sick like that,

130
00:08:15,530 --> 00:08:17,700
when she barely even belongs
outside a hospital?

131
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:20,970
Director Joo,

132
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,180
why don't you see
if you can persuade him?

133
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,580
Recommend a suitable hospital.

134
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,650
I could try,

135
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:32,720
but Chief Cha isn't easily swayed.

136
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,020
You know how stubborn he is.

137
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:40,930
You're always proactive
when it comes to my wife,

138
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:44,430
so why are you being
so passive about this?

139
00:08:48,770 --> 00:08:52,870
Find a way to get So Yeon
to see a physician of our choosing,

140
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:55,310
and at the next
shareholders' meeting,

141
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:58,180
I'll put you
on the board of directors.

142
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,610
Are you serious?

143
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:04,380
Of course.

144
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,690
I'll do my best
to persuade Chief Cha.

145
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:11,290
Good.

146
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:16,760
Seeing her today...

147
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,460
must've given you
an idea of my past.

148
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,300
My life has been much rougher
than you think.

149
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:23,970
So...

150
00:09:24,770 --> 00:09:26,900
be careful while I still treat you
as my superior.

151
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:30,510
Do that, and I'll continue
to show you respect.

152
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,610
Aren't you going to lunch?

153
00:09:35,310 --> 00:09:37,520
We're heading out now.
Why don't you join us?

154
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:39,120
Do you two come to work just to eat?

155
00:09:40,050 --> 00:09:41,490
Learn to read the room.

156
00:09:57,070 --> 00:09:59,100
Hey, sweetheart.

157
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,140
Where are you?

158
00:10:01,010 --> 00:10:03,410
Where else? At home.

159
00:10:04,010 --> 00:10:05,180
Stay right there.

160
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:10,750
Give me your phone.

161
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,150
What?

162
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:15,250
Here.

163
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,490
Sweetheart, what are you doing?

164
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:24,960
Don't ever contact me again.

165
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,670
Your dad came up
with a really great plan.

166
00:10:27,930 --> 00:10:29,430
This time, I'll go after
Ko Eun Seol's family...

167
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,400
Just shut your trap, will you?

168
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:34,670
Ko Eun Seol's cellmate
you met yesterday?

169
00:10:35,170 --> 00:10:36,540
She went straight to Ko Eun Seol.

170
00:10:36,610 --> 00:10:38,810
Ko Eun Seol already knows
everything I'm doing.

171
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:42,610
So what did Ko Eun Seol do
to my little girl?

172
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:44,420
Leave it to me.

173
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:47,020
I should've just listened
to Director Joo back then.

174
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:50,120
What was I expecting
from a scumbag like you anyway?

175
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:55,190
Hae Ra, I'm your dad.

176
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:56,660
Forget it.

177
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,130
Never contact me again.

178
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:12,840
Hae Ra, I'm your dad.

179
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,950
I'll fix everything for you.

180
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:19,780
Ko Eun Seol,
I'll tear you down no matter what.

181
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:22,520
Our Hae Ra is
the only daughter of Cheongma.

182
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:26,320
I'm your father!

183
00:11:30,090 --> 00:11:32,260
If the mistress lives with you,

184
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,900
that gives us a huge advantage.

185
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:38,370
I know this is hard on you, ma'am,

186
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:41,040
but securing key evidence
comes first right now.

187
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:43,510
Right.

188
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:48,010
We should be able
to finish setting up...

189
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:49,280
before the family gets home.

190
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,870
Thank you so much...

191
00:12:12,870 --> 00:12:15,340
for taking such good care
of my mother.

192
00:12:17,010 --> 00:12:18,040
Please bear with her...

193
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:21,350
until I get this whole situation
sorted out.

194
00:12:22,210 --> 00:12:23,950
Just relax,

195
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,720
and think of it
as her visiting a friend's house.

196
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:30,960
Besides, So Yeon really vibes well
with our family.

197
00:12:31,090 --> 00:12:32,420
And with my mother...

198
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:36,560
They seem to hit it off really well,
so don't worry about it.

199
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,860
- Don't worry too much.
- That's right.

200
00:12:38,930 --> 00:12:41,830
As long as you pay us generously
when she leaves,

201
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:43,430
we're fine with whatever.

202
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:45,540
She's only joking. Mom, stop.

203
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:46,970
Fine.

204
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,040
Didn't you say you've known Eun Seol
since high school?

205
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:52,310
Then you two go way back.

206
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:54,450
That's right.

207
00:12:55,110 --> 00:12:56,780
Eun Seol told us...

208
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,220
you've been looking out for her
at work.

209
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,390
So of course we should help.

210
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:04,260
Don't feel like you're imposing.

211
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,990
He's right, Mr. Seok Jin.

212
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,930
Don't stress about it.

213
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:14,770
I'm really comfortable staying here,

214
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:19,640
and playing card games with Ms. Wang
is a lot of fun.

215
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:23,370
See? I told you you'd be
a bad influence on So Yeon.

216
00:13:23,370 --> 00:13:26,280
That's just how life is.

217
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,710
You should appreciate
some traditional Asian art...

218
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,850
and enjoy
the artistic pleasures of life.

219
00:13:30,950 --> 00:13:35,450
Ms. Wang, how about we play
this game again tomorrow?

220
00:13:37,490 --> 00:13:39,160
Is it really that much fun?

221
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:41,430
Yes, it's a blast.

222
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:44,560
I will teach you tomorrow,
nice lady.

223
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,200
So Yeon is completely hooked.

224
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,800
- Like that.
- This will soon be a gambling den.

225
00:13:52,170 --> 00:13:55,010
By the way, Mr. Seok Jin,

226
00:13:55,570 --> 00:13:57,340
you look like you lost some weight.

227
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:59,940
Have you been eating properly?

228
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,650
Of course. There's no need
to worry about your son.

229
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,750
You're eating well too, right, Mom?

230
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:07,590
Yes.

231
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:09,790
The food doesn't taste good,

232
00:14:09,950 --> 00:14:12,720
but I put up with it
and make sure to eat well anyway.

233
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:16,630
By the way, Mom,

234
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:22,000
did you happen to keep
the diaries or notebooks Dad had?

235
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,770
You hardly threw away
any of his things.

236
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,300
Well...

237
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:28,340
His notebook?

238
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:30,640
Yes, there's something
I need to check.

239
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:33,280
Well, his notebook...

240
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,410
I don't know.

241
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:39,650
I really have no idea.

242
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:40,920
All right.

243
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:42,690
I'll look for it myself.

244
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,300
No...

245
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,080
(Inventory Shrinkage Rate)

246
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,920
No, he must never find this.

247
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:23,660
If he finds this,
Seok Jin will be in danger.

248
00:15:34,770 --> 00:15:36,110
No...

249
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:42,780
Wait, what is all this?

250
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:45,580
You said you wanted
home-cooked food.

251
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:50,120
Hold on, did you prepare
all of this just for me?

252
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,560
Don't get too excited.

253
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,890
It might not taste
as good as it looks.

254
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:56,390
Dig in while it's warm.

255
00:15:56,530 --> 00:15:59,730
Did you prepare all this
because of what I said yesterday?

256
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:00,930
Yes.

257
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:03,370
I've been thinking a lot
about my mom lately,

258
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:06,270
and I've missed her cooking.

259
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:10,040
I tried recreating her recipes,
so I can't guarantee how it tastes.

260
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:13,910
Thank you, Eun Seol.

261
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:29,290
Hold on.

262
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,500
Are you crying?

263
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:36,170
No, something just got in my eye.

264
00:16:38,870 --> 00:16:41,270
This food will be very easy
on your stomach.

265
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:44,040
My mom used to say...

266
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:47,080
food cooked with love
is easy on the stomach.

267
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:51,380
I can't vouch for the taste,
but I poured my heart into it.

268
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:54,550
Dig in already.

269
00:17:03,330 --> 00:17:05,560
(Correctional Scholarship Program,
Round 1 Trainees)

270
00:17:07,770 --> 00:17:09,870
What's this?

271
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:14,040
These are the candidates
for the first round of the program.

272
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,070
There are no follow-up evaluations,

273
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:18,410
so I only gathered the ones
that raised red flags.

274
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:21,980
Among them, this guy Park Ho Jun...

275
00:17:23,350 --> 00:17:24,620
seems the most suspicious.

276
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,480
Could...

277
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:31,190
Director Joo be
plotting something again?

278
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:33,260
You'll need to move
as quickly as possible.

279
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:37,690
Why are you giving this to me?

280
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:39,900
You said I felt like
a little brother to you.

281
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:44,030
You feel like a big sister
to me too, Eun Seol.

282
00:17:48,070 --> 00:17:49,110
Secretary Choi,

283
00:17:49,910 --> 00:17:52,380
are you sure about this?

284
00:17:59,350 --> 00:18:01,990
Honestly, the meat
is a bit salty, though.

285
00:18:04,490 --> 00:18:06,390
Hey, it's so good.

286
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:11,530
Better eat up
before I finish it all. Dig in.

287
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:17,840
Take your time.

288
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:25,710
What is this stinking up the room?
Why are you eating in here?

289
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:29,280
Were you two having lunch?

290
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:31,950
Packed lunches, I see.

291
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:34,120
Did you make this, Eun Seol?

292
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:35,390
Yes.

293
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:37,520
Seems like
you're a pretty great cook.

294
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:40,860
(Correctional Scholarship Program,
Round 1 Trainees)

295
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,000
Well, enjoy your meal, both of you.

296
00:18:48,470 --> 00:18:52,140
Just go out and buy lunch.
Packing one is so pathetic.

297
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,070
Leave the door open
to air out the smell.

298
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:06,980
Right, I can't just count
on Choi Jun Hwan alone.

299
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,790
Let's see.

300
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:13,060
Isn't there anyone more desperate?

301
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:15,360
(Detailed List
of Round 1 Training Candidates)

302
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:18,830
Jang Chil Bok?

303
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,800
Jang Chil Bok?

304
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:24,130
(Scholar Management
and Training Compliance Report)

305
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:29,070
Why are you giving this to me?

306
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:30,710
You said I felt like
a little brother to you.

307
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:33,380
You feel like a big sister
to me too, Eun Seol.

308
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:45,020
Hello, is this
Jungmyeong Industries?

309
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,190
This is
Cheongma Scholarship Foundation.

310
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:51,030
Is Park Ho Jun there by any chance?

311
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:54,000
That jerk barely even shows up
to work anymore.

312
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:56,870
Some kind
of training scholarship program?

313
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:58,740
He said he was
in something like that,

314
00:19:59,370 --> 00:20:01,140
and now he's spending money
like water.

315
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:19,020
(Yuri Adult Gaming Room)

316
00:20:20,690 --> 00:20:21,690
Hello.

317
00:20:24,030 --> 00:20:26,260
I'm from Cheongma
Scholarship Foundation.

318
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,570
You're Park Ho Jun, right?

319
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:46,020
Mr. Jang Chil Bok?

320
00:20:51,390 --> 00:20:54,220
I heard your daughter needs
another surgery.

321
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:58,660
It must be so hard on you,

322
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:01,970
especially without a steady job yet.

323
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:20,120
I'll help you, Chil Bok.

324
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:26,990
I'm on my way back from meeting
the scholarship program candidates.

325
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:28,830
Is that so?

326
00:21:29,030 --> 00:21:32,300
Was there anyone
who required special supervision?

327
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:35,700
Park Ho Jun had a gambling record,
so I watched him closely.

328
00:21:36,070 --> 00:21:37,500
He was illegally cashing in
his voucher card...

329
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:38,840
to feed his gambling habit.

330
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:40,570
Voucher fraud?

331
00:21:41,370 --> 00:21:42,710
Is that even possible?

332
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:45,680
There are brokers
who target voucher cards.

333
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:47,240
I see.

334
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:49,480
So how did you handle it?

335
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,780
I expelled him
from the program immediately.

336
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,120
I submitted it for approval today.

337
00:21:53,380 --> 00:21:54,480
Good job.

338
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:57,320
If it weren't for you,
it could've turned into a disaster.

339
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:06,160
Did Secretary Choi leak
the info to me first,

340
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:09,030
knowing Director Joo
was behind this?

341
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:12,770
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

342
00:22:18,210 --> 00:22:22,080
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation
Young Artist Development Proposal)

343
00:22:46,370 --> 00:22:47,400
Kang Hae Ra,

344
00:22:49,170 --> 00:22:52,280
at the very least,
you shouldn't betray the Chairman.

345
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:58,650
Yes, go ahead, Attorney Baek.

346
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:02,490
You haven't forgotten, have you?
Don't ever let it show.

347
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:06,920
Yes, I'm trying my best to do that.

348
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:09,430
And here's a tip.

349
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:11,860
Let the mistress know
when you'll be out of the house.

350
00:23:12,430 --> 00:23:14,560
If we check the wiretaps and CCTV
from that day,

351
00:23:14,730 --> 00:23:16,630
there's a good chance
we'll find evidence.

352
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,970
All right. I'll try that method.

353
00:23:21,970 --> 00:23:23,510
Thank you, Attorney Baek.

354
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:33,280
Did you call for me, Chairman?

355
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:34,650
Yes.

356
00:23:37,150 --> 00:23:39,320
I have a gathering
with Ms. Yang today.

357
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:41,460
Wasn't that next week?

358
00:23:41,590 --> 00:23:44,660
Everyone had conflicts,
so we moved it up.

359
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:46,700
I see.

360
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:48,470
Go ahead and head home without me.

361
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:50,800
I'll probably be late.

362
00:23:51,070 --> 00:23:52,770
Yes, I'll do that.

363
00:23:56,670 --> 00:23:58,180
Don't let on at all.

364
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:01,710
Just act natural,
like you always do.

365
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,510
And Director Joo,

366
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:06,150
hold off on house hunting for now.

367
00:24:07,250 --> 00:24:08,250
Pardon?

368
00:24:09,290 --> 00:24:12,090
On second thought,
until Hae Ra gets married,

369
00:24:12,490 --> 00:24:14,520
I think she needs your support.

370
00:24:15,130 --> 00:24:17,530
At first,
she wanted you to move out,

371
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:19,830
but it seems she changed her mind.

372
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:21,460
Sure,

373
00:24:22,030 --> 00:24:23,070
will do.

374
00:24:29,410 --> 00:24:30,410
Hae Ra.

375
00:24:31,910 --> 00:24:33,640
Do I make you that uncomfortable?

376
00:24:34,380 --> 00:24:35,750
Where is this coming from
all of a sudden?

377
00:24:36,810 --> 00:24:38,250
Did you tell the Chairman...

378
00:24:39,120 --> 00:24:40,950
to kick me out?

379
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:45,420
That's...

380
00:24:49,760 --> 00:24:50,960
Wasn't that to be expected?

381
00:24:52,300 --> 00:24:55,070
The woman I thought was my nanny
turned out to be my birth mother.

382
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:58,170
Of course it's awkward.

383
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:03,610
Then, why did you change your mind?

384
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:09,350
Ko Eun Seol's the real daughter,

385
00:25:09,780 --> 00:25:11,050
and we were swapped, right?

386
00:25:12,350 --> 00:25:15,050
Then I need your help
to protect my position.

387
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,920
Don't think it's because
I'm fond of you.

388
00:25:18,990 --> 00:25:20,390
This is just about survival.

389
00:25:22,530 --> 00:25:23,530
Fine,

390
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:25,430
that's good enough.

391
00:25:27,130 --> 00:25:28,800
You're going to survive here...

392
00:25:29,630 --> 00:25:31,200
and take over Cheongma.

393
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:34,440
I'll stay by your side and help you.

394
00:25:35,170 --> 00:25:36,610
For the rest of my life,
just like I am now.

395
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:40,940
Can I...

396
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,480
really trust you?

397
00:25:44,950 --> 00:25:45,950
Of course.

398
00:26:05,700 --> 00:26:08,870
(Shocking! The Cheongma Scholarship,
A Breeding Ground for Criminals?)

399
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:13,110
What is all this?

400
00:26:18,110 --> 00:26:21,580
My gosh. Ma'am, are you all right?

401
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,320
Are you hurt anywhere?

402
00:26:37,330 --> 00:26:39,400
- Eun Seol.
- What is all this?

403
00:26:40,470 --> 00:26:42,310
You said it was
Park Ho Jun for sure!

404
00:26:43,610 --> 00:26:44,870
I think there was
a misunderstanding.

405
00:26:45,080 --> 00:26:47,140
Director Joo suddenly
switched the target.

406
00:26:49,510 --> 00:26:51,950
What on earth are you
and Director Joo plotting?

407
00:26:57,820 --> 00:26:58,860
Why...

408
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:01,360
Just why are you doing this?

409
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:04,930
What do you get out of doing this,
Secretary Choi?

410
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:07,960
I'm sorry, Eun Seol.

411
00:27:22,710 --> 00:27:24,480
This isn't the recipient
we agreed on.

412
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:27,880
Why is it suddenly Jang Chil Bok
instead of Park Ho Jun?

413
00:27:29,050 --> 00:27:31,590
Every lie has a reason behind it.

414
00:27:32,490 --> 00:27:34,190
Between a gambling addict...

415
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:36,530
and a father desperate to cover
his daughter's surgery costs,

416
00:27:36,890 --> 00:27:38,190
who would be more desperate?

417
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:39,900
Even so, this is...

418
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:43,870
This isn't what we agreed on.

419
00:27:45,100 --> 00:27:46,100
What's wrong?

420
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:48,610
Did you make a promise to someone?

421
00:27:50,540 --> 00:27:52,480
Ko Eun Seol, perhaps?

422
00:27:57,980 --> 00:27:58,980
Jun Hwan,

423
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:01,680
just listen to me.

424
00:28:03,690 --> 00:28:06,820
You are the one
who killed Seo Hyun Jae,

425
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:10,930
and right now Eun Seol is dead set
on tracking the killer down.

426
00:28:11,530 --> 00:28:14,500
How can you stomach the lunch
she packed for you?

427
00:28:16,030 --> 00:28:18,870
Take this chance
to distance yourself from her.

428
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:22,710
I'm only looking out for you.

429
00:28:24,010 --> 00:28:27,480
Since you can't end things yourself,
I'm doing it for you.

430
00:28:28,380 --> 00:28:29,450
Do you follow me?

431
00:28:33,380 --> 00:28:35,850
(Cheongma Foundation in Crisis,
Cash-out Fraud Scandal)

432
00:28:45,460 --> 00:28:46,460
Sir.

433
00:28:49,530 --> 00:28:51,870
Chief Cha, what brings you here?

434
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:55,440
I had no idea you came
to this sauna too.

435
00:28:57,010 --> 00:28:58,170
Hae Ra mentioned...

436
00:28:58,740 --> 00:29:00,410
you're a regular here.

437
00:29:03,780 --> 00:29:05,520
Did something good happen?

438
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:07,850
You look very relaxed.

439
00:29:08,690 --> 00:29:12,190
Well, yes.
I guess you could say that.

440
00:29:15,090 --> 00:29:16,330
Do you come here often?

441
00:29:17,590 --> 00:29:19,200
Yes, once in a while.

442
00:29:19,930 --> 00:29:22,470
When things aren't going well,

443
00:29:23,270 --> 00:29:24,270
or like today,

444
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:28,170
when things just fall into place.

445
00:29:28,610 --> 00:29:29,710
That's when I come.

446
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:34,640
Coming here relaxes
both my body and mind.

447
00:29:36,050 --> 00:29:37,050
I see.

448
00:29:41,420 --> 00:29:42,790
So did you ask Hae Ra...

449
00:29:43,690 --> 00:29:45,520
and come all the way here to see me?

450
00:29:47,460 --> 00:29:48,490
Yes.

451
00:29:49,330 --> 00:29:51,290
I wanted to spend some time
with you, sir.

452
00:29:52,030 --> 00:29:53,030
Right.

453
00:29:53,830 --> 00:29:55,470
A sauna session
with my future son-in-law.

454
00:29:56,930 --> 00:29:58,370
Not bad.

455
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:05,980
Actually,

456
00:30:06,980 --> 00:30:09,180
there's something
I'd like to ask you.

457
00:30:10,380 --> 00:30:11,410
Sure.

458
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,380
Ask me anything.

459
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:16,420
It's about
Managing Director Oh Tae Seop.

460
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:24,690
Turns out he started at Cheongma's
subcontracted logistics center.

461
00:30:27,130 --> 00:30:28,130
Right.

462
00:30:29,730 --> 00:30:31,630
Yes, that's right.

463
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:37,840
Isn't he the one responsible
for what happened to my father?

464
00:30:40,010 --> 00:30:41,910
How could the person
who killed my father...

465
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:45,680
end up as managing director
at Cheongma?

466
00:30:56,230 --> 00:30:58,430
My first scholarship program...

467
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:01,000
can't end like this.

468
00:31:01,930 --> 00:31:03,970
We have to save it, no matter what.

469
00:31:06,140 --> 00:31:07,140
Ma'am.

470
00:31:08,710 --> 00:31:10,070
Take a look at this.

471
00:31:15,010 --> 00:31:16,680
What's this?

472
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:20,080
It's a new scholarship program.

473
00:31:21,350 --> 00:31:23,690
Director Joo and Team Leader Kang
have been preparing this.

474
00:31:26,090 --> 00:31:28,790
Then putting Hae Ra in my place...

475
00:31:29,290 --> 00:31:31,560
while I was out of the office
was also...

476
00:31:31,930 --> 00:31:32,930
Yes.

477
00:31:33,730 --> 00:31:35,930
Director Joo planned
your abuse-of-power scandal,

478
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:37,470
and everything...

479
00:31:38,670 --> 00:31:40,270
that followed.

480
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,170
Then what do we do?

481
00:31:44,340 --> 00:31:46,580
Is this how
the scholarship program ends?

482
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:49,850
It looks that way.

483
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:52,550
At the interim board meeting,

484
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:55,690
they're going to shut down
the scholarship program.

485
00:31:55,950 --> 00:31:56,990
If that happens,

486
00:31:58,420 --> 00:32:00,560
there's really nothing we can do.

487
00:32:08,200 --> 00:32:12,070
An interim board meeting
was actually called.

488
00:32:14,540 --> 00:32:15,670
It was...

489
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:19,580
the most rewarding thing
I've ever done.

490
00:32:21,710 --> 00:32:23,050
Having my first project...

491
00:32:25,080 --> 00:32:26,480
end like this...

492
00:32:28,250 --> 00:32:29,720
is utterly heartbreaking.

493
00:32:31,650 --> 00:32:32,690
I'll make sure...

494
00:32:34,020 --> 00:32:35,530
we get it back.

495
00:32:45,100 --> 00:32:46,100
Goodness.

496
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:48,040
What brings my daughter here?

497
00:32:50,810 --> 00:32:51,870
What is the meaning of all this?

498
00:32:53,580 --> 00:32:54,610
Tell me about it.

499
00:32:55,110 --> 00:32:57,410
The Chairman must be
pretty heartbroken.

500
00:32:58,350 --> 00:33:00,220
I bet you're upset about this too.

501
00:33:01,080 --> 00:33:04,550
You built that scholarship program
entirely through your own legwork.

502
00:33:05,460 --> 00:33:07,260
It's truly unfortunate.

503
00:33:09,260 --> 00:33:11,490
Come get a hug from your mom.

504
00:33:15,570 --> 00:33:17,170
What do you want from me?

505
00:33:18,530 --> 00:33:19,740
What do I want?

506
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:22,310
My daughter's happiness?

507
00:33:22,510 --> 00:33:25,170
What do you really want from me?

508
00:33:48,260 --> 00:33:51,830
(A Trap Called Desire)

509
00:33:52,240 --> 00:33:55,540
I should go right now and drag
Ko Eun Seol back by the hair.

510
00:33:55,670 --> 00:33:57,310
This is the only way, right?

511
00:33:57,310 --> 00:33:59,540
Is the Acting Chairman ready?

512
00:33:59,610 --> 00:34:02,040
You had better brace yourself
as well, Hae Ra.

513
00:34:02,110 --> 00:34:05,720
Isn't promoting him
to managing director a little much?

514
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:08,550
Is being all slow and clueless
just an act?

515
00:34:08,620 --> 00:34:10,720
She's not dim-witted at all.

516
00:34:11,090 --> 00:34:14,190
What did I just hear?
That can't be true.

517
00:34:14,660 --> 00:34:16,790
Hae Ra's mom,
let's team up from now on.

518
00:34:16,860 --> 00:34:18,490
Will you shut your mouth?

519
00:34:18,490 --> 00:34:20,100
Just how much do you know?

520
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:22,000
Why did you pretend to be my mom?

521
00:34:22,170 --> 00:34:24,170
I bet you want to know
what I've found out.

522
00:34:24,230 --> 00:34:26,240
Don't push your luck.

523
00:34:26,370 --> 00:34:29,270
Why won't you answer?
Whose daughter are you?

524
00:34:30,740 --> 00:34:32,740
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
